{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>One who sacrifices to elohim shall be proscribed (יָחֳרָם).</b> Because the second commandment warned against idolatry in general terms and did not specify the punishment, therefore it is specified here that he is liable to death, in the manner of what is written (Leviticus 27:29): ״אך כל חרם אשר יחרם מן האדם לא יפדה מות יומת״. And it says יחרם — measure for measure: he sacrifices to what is proscribed (חרם), as is said (Deuteronomy 7:26): ״והיית חרם כמוהו״ — and you shall be proscribed like it, etc. — for it is חרם, and therefore יחרם. And further, it includes both the sacrificer and the sacrifice, for it too is forbidden for benefit. And the fact that it mentioned slaughter (זביחה) — the same law applies to bowing, to libation, to incense, and to the other forms of worship; but one who honors, spreads a garment, embraces, or kisses is not liable to death for worship not according to its manner (שלא כדרכה); but according to its manner (כדרכה), if its manner of worship is in such, he is liable to death in every case, even one who exposes himself for exposure (פוער עצמו לפעור). Rashi, of blessed memory, explained: לאלהים — with a pataḥ under the lamed — meaning those concerning whom you were warned at Sinai: ״לא יהיה לך אלהים אחרים״ — and they are the angels." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the word לאלהים alludes to the secret of the sacrifices, in the manner of what is written (Numbers 28:2): ״את קרבני לחמי לאשי״. And our Sages of blessed memory interpreted: I might think לחמי — the verse says לאשי — you assign them as offerings of fire; and this is true, but the intention is toward the unique Name, and this is why it states here בלתי לה' לבדו — to HaShem alone — and therefore Onkelos translated: אלהן לשמא דה' בלחודוהי — to the name of YHWH alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:01.283530375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}